{
 "kind": "refuse",
 "message": "Hi Yusuf, I can't do this. I won't share your TMS login or reset your password so Kevin can use your account. Under POL-SEC-01, accounts are personal: passwords must never be shared and nobody may log in as someone else. Resetting your password to send to Kevin would break that rule too.\n\nHere are some options for covering your loads while you're out on Thursday and Friday:\n- Kevin can request his own TMS access. Under POL-ACC-01, an employee can ask for access for themselves, and standard systems like TMS are approved by the employee's manager (usually within 1 business day). If you want, Kevin can message me directly and I'll file that request for him.\n- Your manager can arrange cover, for example by asking Kevin to take over your loads through the usual handover process.\n\nIf you have any questions about your own access or account, I can help with those.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-SEC-01",
  "POL-ACC-01"
 ]
}
